        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Baryshnikov, Mark Morris, George Gershwin\n- Works: Three Preludes\n- Organizations: New York City Ballet\n- Places: New York State Theater, Lincoln Center\n- Topics: ballet, dance, choreography\n\nFacts:\n- Mikhail Baryshnikov was born on January 27, 1948, and he is a Soviet and American dancer, choreographer, and actor.\n- Mikhail Baryshnikov is nicknamed \"Misha.\"\n- Three Preludes is a ballet made for Mikhail Baryshnikov by Mark Morris to music by George Gershwin.\n- Three Preludes was created for Mark Morris's own company and was presented as a pièce d'occasion by the New York City Ballet.\n- The performance of Three Preludes took place on June 16, 1992, at the New York State Theater in Lincoln Center.",
